# Tutorial 02 — driving the app from the command line.
title: The command line
summary: Commands, aliases, coordinates, options, repeat and undo
---
open new
zoom window -1000,-1500 15000,8500
caption "Just start typing" "Commands go straight to the command line; Enter or Space confirms"
wait 1.5
type LINE 0,0 4000,0 ;
note "Each prompt waits for a point, a value or an [option]" at commandline for 3.5
wait 2.5
caption "Aliases" "L is LINE, C is CIRCLE, REC is RECTANG, PL is PLINE…"
type L 0,1000 3000,1000 ;
type C 6000,1200 900
wait 1.5
caption "Absolute coordinates" "x,y measured from the origin"
type REC 8500,0 12500,2500
wait 1.5
caption "Relative coordinates" "@dx,dy measured from the last point"
type PL 0,3000 @3000,0 @0,1500 @-3000,0 C
wait 1.5
caption "Polar coordinates" "@distance<angle, angles in degrees counter-clockwise"
type LINE 4000,3000 @2500<30 @2500<-30 ;
wait 1.5
caption "Options" "Type the capital letters of an option: D for Diameter"
type CIRCLE 10500,5000 D 1800
note "D switched the prompt from radius to diameter" at 10500,5900 for 3
wait 3
caption "Enter repeats the last command" "An empty Enter starts CIRCLE again"
enter
type 13500,5000 600
wait 1.5
caption "Undo and redo" "U undoes the last command, REDO brings it back"
type U
wait 1.2
type REDO
wait 1.2
caption "Units and arithmetic" "2.5m, 30cm, 3'6\" and 2400/2 are all valid input"
type LINE 0,6000 @2.5m<0 @2400/2<90 ;
wait 2
caption "History" "↑ and ↓ recall earlier lines; F2 shows the whole history"
click panel History
wait 3
click panel Properties
caption "Next: drawing basics" "Tutorial 03 covers snaps, ortho, trim, offset and fillet"
wait 3
